      "originalText": "each process thinks it has full access to memory - it has its own VAS\nfor each process, addressing starts at 0\ngives the impression to have more (virtual) memory than the actual available system physical memory\ncan share virtual memory with other processes\neach process is isolated in its own virtual address space - isolation, security",
